{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793799844,"nonce":"Rbej05GqizIpCmgmZ5HYGI2T50w=","title":"HIR: forward scalar stores through single-entry regions","message":"Lua method_call retains repeated field loads after inlining even when the same address was just stored. Source-location global stores also invalidate the available field value although its allocation cannot overlap module-global storage. The final Cranelift code consequently keeps ten load/flip/store sequences in the Toggle loop; LuaJIT forwards and folds this work (comparison in 53de3273d900a43d6ba866646d99875e82972744471affd0c481d6bc1ebd90bf).\n\nExtend load_cse to forward a same-typed scalar store to a later load within existing single-entry regions. Keep calls, volatile/atomic operations, joins, backedges, partial writes and unknown aliases as barriers. A fresh allocation versus a module global is a disjointness proof; unrelated SSA ids by themselves are not. Do not forward aggregate pointer carriers or reinterpret stored bytes as another type.\n\nValidate alias and control-flow cases in the interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM; compare cooled NUC frozen binaries before corpus runs; run full pinned official TypeScript regression baseline before committing. General loop-carried field promotion and source-location store elimination remain separate follow-ups.","files":null}]}